/*
 * Callexpander - expands all call-like expressions into YIL values and
 * instructions.
 *
 * The CallExpander lowers high-level semantic call nodes into concrete YIL
 * constructs. It ensures:
 *
 *   - calls are evaluated exactly once,
 *   - side-effects are preserved,
 *   - temporary variables are created when required,
 *   - destructors are inserted for movable values,
 *   - constructor, method, function-pointer and prototype calls are expanded
 *     into their canonical YIL form.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::lint::expander::value::call
 * @File: ymirc/lint/expander/value/call.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-06-22
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
